From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <106575910+KRRT7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:07:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Live: real-time scheduling hints on Windows

Windows ran the voice worker and face-swap threads at normal priority,
competing with the browser, OBS or a game, and Windows 11 could move
them to efficiency cores (EcoQoS) when the window lost focus.

Add rvc/lib/win_rt.py (ctypes only, no-op off Windows, never raises):
- boost_thread(task) registers the thread with MMCSS.
- boost_process() raises to ABOVE_NORMAL and opts out of EcoQoS;
  restore_process() undoes it.

The voice worker process is boosted with its thread as "Pro Audio";
audio callbacks register as "Pro Audio" (WASAPI already does this
inside PortAudio, MME/DirectSound/ASIO did not). The Live session boosts
the app process while it runs and restores it on stop; capture threads
run as "Capture", detect/process as "Games".

Vendored code changed: LiveSession takes an optional thread_hint
callback, called on each worker thread as it starts, so the vendored
package stays independent of Applio.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Applio-Commit: e8ae46da4d1bbcf10d0f28fa850b2cb57c7c37e3
---
 _vendor/modules/live.py | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/_vendor/modules/live.py b/_vendor/modules/live.py
index cc62415..be1161b 100644
--- a/_vendor/modules/live.py
+++ b/_vendor/modules/live.py
@@ -610,8 +610,12 @@ class LiveSession:
         fps: int = 60,
         sinks: Sequence[FrameSink] = (),
         capture_factory: Callable[[int], VideoCapturer] = VideoCapturer,
+        thread_hint: Optional[Callable[[str], None]] = None,
     ):
         self.camera_index = camera_index
+        # Called on each worker thread as it starts, with "capture", "detect"
+        # or "process", so the host can raise its scheduling priority.
+        self._thread_hint = thread_hint
         self.requested = (width, height, fps)
         self.sinks: List[FrameSink] = list(sinks)
         self._capture_factory = capture_factory
@@ -702,7 +706,15 @@ class LiveSession:
 
     # threads
 
+    def _hint(self, role: str) -> None:
+        if self._thread_hint is not None:
+            try:
+                self._thread_hint(role)
+            except Exception:
+                pass  # a scheduling hint must never stop the session
+
     def _capture_loop(self) -> None:
+        self._hint("capture")
         while not self._stop.is_set():
             ret, frame = self._cap.read()
             if not ret:
@@ -717,6 +729,7 @@ class LiveSession:
         self._stop.set()
 
     def _detect_loop(self) -> None:
+        self._hint("detect")
         while not self._stop.is_set():
             try:
                 frame = self._capture_q.get(timeout=0.05)
@@ -737,6 +750,7 @@ class LiveSession:
                     continue
 
     def _process_loop(self) -> None:
+        self._hint("process")
         while not self._stop.is_set():
             try:
                 det = self._detect_q.get(timeout=0.05)
